act. The correction must keep those descriptions accurate, including new submission versus replay.\n\nSecurity: source inspection supports the explicit destination comparisons, exact live hold-owner rule, canonical commit validation and preserved final merge check. The reproduced defect is an availability/recovery failure; no unauthorized merge was demonstrated. Do not repair it by accepting a stale new authorization, trusting a key without payload equality, or weakening the writer/actor boundary. The separately filed HTTP gap remains visible.\n\nSimplification: retain one target-check implementation and one existing accepted-submission replay path. Do not add a second retry store or an extra authorization cycle to work around a failed retry. The scoped unheld/held/legacy documentation is a useful clarification.\n\nValidation limits: reviewed the changed production code and all changed contract pages; both named tests ran through canonical-path overlays in a clean detached checkout. No tracked source changed. I stopped broad validation after this reproducible blocker; this is not a clean full-suite/race verdict. The author's earlier race failure has no retained full trace and remains unattributed; passing reruns do not establish that it was pre-existing. Retain the full trace if it recurs during corrected-head validation.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:d2ed639e81667a3d2442b26a8b2ae21e72c1c6f5","head":"1481eca1272155c6608c5e40f2951d43f7b62400","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:59f20ba2133682bdc2f56935d39560c658dca7db\",\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:6cce36694634deb3d8dd4aa91e3767dc136c7cb4\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:6cce36694634deb3d8dd4aa91e3767dc136c7cb4","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}